<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

<h3>FFmpeg or FFprobe Not Found (Exit Code <code>5</code>)</h3>
<p>
  When FluxEncoder exits with code <code>5</code> (<code>DependencyMissing</code>), confirm both binaries are installed and reachable on <code>PATH</code>, or pass explicit binary paths via <code>--ffmpeg</code> and <code>--ffprobe</code>:
</p>

{{ terminalFrame({
  title: "bash — verify FFmpeg installation",
  stream: "stdout",
  code: "ffmpeg -version
ffprobe -version"
}) }}

<h3>Hardware Encoder Unavailable (Exit Code <code>6</code>)</h3>
<p>
  Hardware encoding requires both an FFmpeg build compiled with the vendor library (<code>hevc_nvenc</code>, <code>hevc_amf</code>, <code>hevc_qsv</code>, <code>hevc_videotoolbox</code>) and a working driver/device on the host. Inspect encoders exposed by the local FFmpeg binary:
</p>

{{ terminalFrame({
  title: "bash — list FFmpeg encoders and hardware accelerators",
  stream: "stdout",
  code: "ffmpeg -hide_banner -encoders
ffmpeg -hide_banner -hwaccels"
}) }}
<p>
  Pass <code>--hardware auto</code> or <code>--hardware-fallback</code> to allow FluxEncoder to fall back to software encoding when the hardware test encode fails, or use <code>--hardware cpu</code> explicitly.
</p>
